// M9 correctly rounded binary64 pow.
//
// Write |x| = m 2^e with m in [sqrt2/2, sqrt2), and z = y log2|x| = y e + y L
// with L = log2(m). Then |x|^y = 2^k exp2(r) with k = round(z), r = z - k.
//
// L comes from the 192-bit format: s = (m - 1) / (m + 1) to 2^-189, the
// 38-term atanh sum (tail below 2^-199.5, Horner damped by s^2 < 2^-5), and
// the 192-bit 2/ln2, so L is within 2^-186 relative. Since m is chosen in
// [sqrt2/2, sqrt2), |e + L| >= |e|/2, so |y L| <= |z| and the products need
// no cancellation analysis. y e is exact. z is therefore within
// 2^11 * 2^-186 = 2^-175 absolute for every |z| < 2048, and r = z - k is
// exact. r is truncated to 128 bits (2^-129 absolute) and exp2(r) evaluated
// on the exp polynomial as in exp2, within 2^-119.9 relative. The result is
// within 2^-119.8 relative, against the 2^-116 certification margin.
//
// pow is not transcendental on every input: x^y is rational, and may then be
// exactly representable or exactly halfway, when |x| = X 2^E (X odd) is a
// perfect 2^k-th power and y = n / 2^k. With X > 1 that needs X >= 3^(2^k),
// so k <= 5, and y > 0. Those cases are computed exactly in integers and
// rounded exactly; every other x^y is irrational or a non-dyadic rational
// and is evaluated as above.

// Generated by tools/m9/generate-pow-constants.py. Do not edit by hand.
constant soft_wide3 SOFT_POW_TWO_OVER_LN2 = soft_wide3{0xb8aa3b295c17f0bbul, 0xbe87fed0691d3e88ul, 0xeb577aa8dd695a58ul, 2, false};
